Z||000000||mrgone||10-23-2001||03:41 AM||||Wasn't doing anything abusive at the time, went for a 1st to 2nd shift, clutch went soft, car stuck in first. i stopped, shut the car off. the check engine light came on, (i cant wait to check for codes)<BR>The car will go through the gears when its turned off and clutch in. When i drive, and go to stop, the clutch doesnt make the car go out of gear, it starts to stall when the car slows. I can only move the car if i put it in gear with the car off, and start it. But then I cant get it out of gear.<P>I cant afford this, today was the first day I put my insurance back on.<P>I drove it in first gear to the shop. Its 4am and i just... feel like crap. I didnt want this to happen.<P>Any insight on the problem? From the info can you tell exactly whats wrong, and maybe and estimate (canadian$) of the repair?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||10-23-2001||09:14 AM||||I think it's the weather . . .<P>My clutch is doing the same thing, and I see lots of other messages here from people with clutch problems.  This seems to happen when cold temperatures arrive.<P>The symptoms sound like clutch hydraulics; however, after replacing my master and slave cylinders, I'm about to convince myself that my problem is the clutch itself.<P>If you decide to fix this yourself, check Fiero Store for prices; they charge about the same as local parts stores.  (Here, anyhow.)<P>Good luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||10-23-2001||10:49 AM||||mrgone - sounds to me like you sprung a leak in your clutch hydraulics, or maybe one of the seals got torn or worn out in the clutch master or slave cylinders.<P>With air (or a lack of fluid) in the system, the slave cylinder doesn't get enough "throw" to completely disengage the clutch, so gears are still turning (or are not released to move freely) to allow you to move the shift lever around smoothly between the gear positions. <P>From what you've said, I don't think anything is wrong with the clutch itself - just the hydraulics. Much easier to fix than the clutch itself.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||10:57 AM||||Try bleeding the clutch system. <P>Use these instructions. <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch4.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch4.htm</A> ||||reg||1
